===============================================================================
                       VLAN TRAFFIC CONTROL OPERATOR
                         RELEASE & BUILD GUIDELINES
===============================================================================

1. OVERVIEW & SCOPE OF release.sh
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `release.sh` script is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for publishing official 
production releases of the VLAN Traffic Control Operator.

Scope of `release.sh`:
  • Version Bumping: Executes `bump-to-new-version.sh` and syncs image tags across
    Go code, CRDs, deployment manifests, and OLM bases.
  • Pre-flight Checks: Validates target version alignment across key files.
  • Manifest & Bundle Generation: Runs `make generate`, `make manifests`, and 
    `operator-sdk generate bundle` to produce clean OLM bundle artifacts.
  • Container Image Build & Push (GHCR):
      - Operator Manager Image (`vlan-traffic-control-operator:vX.Y.Z`)
      - Node Agent Image      (`vlan-traffic-control-agent:vX.Y.Z`)
      - OLM Bundle Image      (`vlan-traffic-control-bundle:vX.Y.Z`)
  • File-Based Catalog (FBC): Renders `catalog/index.json`, injects display 
    icons, and builds/pushes the Catalog Index image 
    (`vlan-traffic-control-catalog:vX.Y.Z`).


2. WHEN TO USE release.sh
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
USE release.sh WHEN:
  ✔ Cutting a new release (e.g., upgrading from v0.2.50 to v0.2.51).
  ✔ Pushing update catalogs to OpenShift OperatorHub / OLM.
  ✔ Publishing official container images to GitHub Container Registry (GHCR).

DO NOT USE release.sh FOR:
  ✖ Daily local Go code debugging or running unit/integration tests.
  ✖ Quick local CRD/operator testing (use standard `make install` or `make run`).


3. PREREQUISITES BEFORE RUNNING
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Authenticated to Container Registry (`podman login ghcr.io`).
  • `operator-sdk`, `opm`, `podman`, `python3`, and `jq` installed in PATH.
  • Clean git working state (recommended).
  • If replacing a failed cluster deployment during testing, clean stale OLM 
    resources on OpenShift first:
      $ oc delete csv vlan-traffic-control.v<OLD_VERSION> -n openshift-vlan-tc-operator
      $ oc delete deployment vlan-traffic-control-manager -n openshift-vlan-tc-operator


4. USAGE SYNTAX
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Syntax:
    ./release.sh <OLD_VERSION> <NEW_VERSION>

  Example:
    ./release.sh 0.2.50 0.2.51


5. SCRIPT DEPENDENCIES & CLEANUP
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • `bump-to-new-version.sh` : REQUIRED (called automatically in Step 1).
  • `config/deploy/manager.yaml` : REQUIRED (source manifest for manager deployment).
  • `config/manifests/bases/vlan-traffic-control.clusterserviceversion.yaml` : 
    REQUIRED (must have `deployments: []` so OLM bundles generate cleanly).
  • Note: `build-and-deploy.sh` has been removed from the repository. All 
    manifest generation and image publishing flow strictly through `release.sh`.
===============================================================================
